| 7 | 20 | 80 | $4,400 | $147 | $199 | $4,746 |
| 8 | 22 | 98 | $5,390 | $98 | $0 | $5,488 |
| 9 | 25 | 119 | $6,545 | $147 | $199 | $6,891 |
| 10 | 28 | 142 | $7,810 | $98 | $0 | $7,908 |
| 11 | 30 | 167 | $9,185 | $147 | $199 | $9,531 |
| 12 | 35 | 198 | $10,890 | $98 | $0 | $10,988 |

### Year 1 Summary
- Total Revenue: ~$67,350
- Ending MRR: $10,890
- Total Customers: 198 active subscribers
- Revenue Mix: Subscription 84%, Template Pack 2.3%, Consulting 1.8%

### Conservative vs Aggressive Scenarios

| Metric | Conservative | Base | Aggressive |
|--------|--------------|------|------------|
| Month 6 MRR | $2,000 | $3,465 | $5,500 |
| Year 1 Revenue | $45,000 | $67,350 | $110,000 |
| Ending Customers | 120 | 198 | 350 |

---

## 5. IMPLEMENTATION ROADMAP

### Phase 1: Launch (Weeks 1-4)
- Set up Stripe account + API keys
- Create 3 pricing tiers in Stripe
- Build landing page with pricing section
- Enable Stripe Customer Portal
- Launch with Starter + Pro tiers only

### Phase 2: Stabilize (Months 2-3)
- Add Template Pack via Gumroad/Stripe Link
- Implement usage tracking (invoice counts)
- Add Agency tier when you have 10+ Pro customers asking for more

### Phase 3: Scale (Months 4-6)
- Add annual billing option (2 months free discount)
- Introduce consulting for high-touch onboarding
- Add usage-based overage for heavy users

---

## 6. KEY METRICS TO TRACK

| Metric | Target | Why It Matters |
|--------|--------|----------------|
| MRR Growth Rate | 15-20% mo/mo | Healthy SaaS growth |
| Churn Rate | <5% monthly | Indicates product-market fit |
| CAC (Customer Acquisition Cost) | <$100 | Should be <25% of LTV |
| LTV (Lifetime Value) | >$600 | Aim for LTV:CAC > 3:1 |
| Activation Rate | >40% | Users who complete onboarding |

---

